IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`
IMPORT `sgba-sched`
IMPORT `sgba-p1-defs`
IMPORT `sgba-p5-apparatus`
IMPORT `sgba-p11-offences`
IMPORT `sgba-i-tvro-regs`

-- QUARANTINED (name starts sgba-tv-): the Interpretation Act s 9A question for the Broadcasting Act side of the question, and its tests.
-- The Interpretation Act 1965 is encoded in this repository at subjects/sg/interpretation-act/encodings/legalese-sonnet-5.5/ (s 9A included); it is CITED here, not re-encoded
-- (stable l4 cannot IMPORT across folders: see NOTES.md, "Cross-folder links").
-- s 9A(1): a court may prefer the purposive reading. s 9A(2): it may look at extrinsic material to confirm the ordinary meaning or, where that meaning is ambiguous or leads to a
-- result that is manifestly absurd or unreasonable, to find the meaning. Encoded as what it is: a QUESTION A COURT MAY WEIGH, never a rule that flips the literal answer.
-- Nothing in this file changes any literal answer of layer 1. The function takes the literal answer (an offence, or NOTHING) and says only whether the literal answer is in the territory
-- s 9A(2)(b)(ii) names, using a structural marker the text can bear: that on the literal reading the person has no lawful way to comply.
-- Whether that makes the result "manifestly absurd or unreasonable" is for the court; this file does not say.

§ `Is there a lawful way to comply? (the marker)`

-- The person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1) when no licence can be granted to the person (reg 3(2)) and no exemption covers the person (s 20(3), s 20(4), a s 60(b) order).
-- NOTHING where the deposited text of either instrument does not cover the date.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person is an institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not required to obtain a licence by section 20(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, the apparatus or the class is exempt under section 20(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted by an order under section 60(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1), on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 3(2) the person may be granted a licence, on` d `the person is an institution`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST licensable THEN
        IF `the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` d
        THEN JUST ((NOT licensable) AND (NOT `the person is not required to obtain a licence by section 20(3)`) AND (NOT `the person, the apparatus or the class is exempt under section 20(4)`) AND (NOT `the person is exempted by an order under section 60(b)`))
        ELSE NOTHING

§ `Is the literal reading in the territory section 9A(2)(b)(ii) names?`

GIVEN `the literal answer: the person commits an offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has no lawful way to comply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the literal reading is in the territory that Interpretation Act section 9A(2)(b)(ii) names, which a court may weigh` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the literal answer: the person commits an offence`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST offence THEN
        CONSIDER `the person has no lawful way to comply`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST noWay THEN JUST (offence AND noWay)

§ `Tests: the literal answer is never changed by the marker`

-- An individual with a satellite receiving system at home, receiving services, no licence, no exemption, on 1 June 2025: literal answer an offence (s 47), and no lawful way to comply.
#ASSERT `s 47 the person is guilty of an offence` (`s 20(1) the person contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c), on` (Date 1 6 2025) (Apparatus WITH `capable of reception of a broadcasting service` IS TRUE, `capable of direct reception from a satellite` IS TRUE) (`Dealing with apparatus` WITH `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore` IS FALSE, `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale` IS FALSE, `operates it` IS TRUE, `has it` IS FALSE, `the place is premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person` IS TRUE, `broadcasting services are received on or by it` IS TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1), on` (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the literal reading is in the territory that Interpretation Act section 9A(2)(b)(ii) names, which a court may weigh` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an institution can be licensed: a lawful way exists, so the marker is not met, and the literal answer is untouched
#ASSERT `the person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1), on` (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the literal reading is in the territory that Interpretation Act section 9A(2)(b)(ii) names, which a court may weigh` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an exemption is a lawful way
#ASSERT `the person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1), on` (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1), on` (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1), on` (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- where the literal answer is not covered, the territory question is not covered
#ASSERT `the literal reading is in the territory that Interpretation Act section 9A(2)(b)(ii) names, which a court may weigh` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the literal reading is in the territory that Interpretation Act section 9A(2)(b)(ii) names, which a court may weigh` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1), on` (Date 24 9 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1), on` (Date 28 2 2004) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person has no lawful way to comply with section 20(1), on` (Date 5 11 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an offence the literal answer does not find: the territory is not reached
#ASSERT `the literal reading is in the territory that Interpretation Act section 9A(2)(b)(ii) names, which a court may weigh` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
